""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"en\""},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"En\""},{"type":"text","text":" are equivalent and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"en_US\""},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"en-US\""},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["    The locale is fixed for the lifetime of the returned instance. Passing a different `locale` for an","    already initialized `channelKey` has no effect - call `Zendesk.invalidate()` first, then `initialize`","    with the new locale.","","    Backend content — bot replies, settings and campaigns — follows this locale, as does the","    UIKit messaging interface (labels, buttons, error messages, VoiceOver descriptions, dates and","    plural forms). Lookup falls back from an exact match (`\"en-AU\"`) to the closest available","    translation (`\"en-GB\"`) and finally to the SDK's built-in English. Your app's own string","    overrides in `Bundle.main` continue to take precedence for the chosen locale.","","    Some things deliberately keep following the device: layout *direction*, Help Center article","    *content*, the Zendesk Voice SDK interface, and regional formatting (calendar, number separators,","    file-size units)."],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Attention","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This method must complete successfully before "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Zendesk.instance"},{"type":"text","text":" can be called."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"After a successful call has been made, calling it again with the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"channelKey"},{"type":"text","text":" will succeed immediately"},{"type":"text","text":" "}